sa1.start.title = Register for Self Assessment
sa1.start.heading = Register for Self Assessment
sa1.start.intro = This service allows you to register for Self Assessment if you need to send a tax return, but are not self-employed. You may need to send a tax return if you:
sa1.start.reasons.director = are a director with untaxed income
sa1.start.reasons.childBenefitCharge = need to pay High Income Child Benefit charge
sa1.start.reasons.ukPropertyIncome = get income from land and property in the UK
sa1.start.reasons.foreignIncome = get taxable foreign income
sa1.start.reasons.trustIncome = get annual income from a trust or settlement
sa1.start.reasons.incomeThresholds = have annual income that has exceeded annual thresholds
sa1.start.reasons.untaxedIncome = have untaxed income that was not collected through your PAYE tax code
sa1.start.reasons.capitalGainsTax = have Capital Gains Tax to pay
sa1.start.directors.heading = Directors
sa1.start.directors.content = If you are a director, you only need to register for Self Assessment if you have untaxed income. Directors with income taxed at source do not need to send a tax return.
sa1.start.childBenefitCharge.heading = High Income Child Benefit Charge
sa1.start.childBenefitCharge.content = For tax years 2024 to 2025 and onwards, you no longer need to register for Self Assessment if the only reason is to pay the High Income Child Benefit Charge.
sa1.start.childBenefitCharge.payeService = You can instead pay the charge using the
sa1.start.childBenefitCharge.payeService.linkText = PAYE High Income Benefit Charge service (opens in new tab)
sa1.start.childBenefitCharge.alternative = If you choose not to use the PAYE service, you are still required to register for Self Assessment and send a tax return to pay the charge.
sa1.start.requirements.heading = What you will need to register
sa1.start.requirements.intro = To use this service, you will need:
sa1.start.requirements.nationalInsuranceNumber = your National Insurance number, if you have one
sa1.start.requirements.incomeOrBenefitDates = the dates of when you started earning untaxed income or received child benefits
sa1.start.requirements.applyForNationalInsuranceNumber = You can
sa1.start.requirements.applyForNationalInsuranceNumber.linkText = apply for a National Insurance number (opens in new tab)
sa1.start.requirements.applyForNationalInsuranceNumber.noNino = if you do not have one.

